commit f7111938e25ea35c7ef5c48ee18b378c61a193a3
Author: Sam <sam@Sams-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 19:27:56 2026 -0500

    qlever: EXP-P2Q fix round for V-P2Q (Q62a): every read surface honours its basis; no ACKed frame can be lost
    
    C1 Datalog inside a transaction waits for the replica's real marker to
       reach sourceK, then fails BasisNotAvailable; the executor's view marks
       the transaction's CAS read set scope-wide.
    C2 the cached replica marker is never trusted for an answer: Datalog,
       dependencyState and drain probe the real marker before and after the
       answer; an idle applier probes it and replays after a regression.
    C3 process-wide registry of open stream directories by realpath plus a
       kernel flock held by a perl helper (R23); explicit takeover flag for
       crash simulations; a failed start releases both.
    M1 segment format 2 checksums its header; refuse to start when the
       WATERMARK names an LSN above the scanned valid end.
    M2 a repository pull beyond lastPositionOf(durableLsn) waits within the
       deadline, then BasisNotAvailable; A0 gets a pure guard (no extra
       request at or below the position it has observed).
    M3 pulls and retraction-target reads fall back to the log when the
       replica is unreachable; Datalog, dependencyState and broker-mode native
       SPARQL fail typed (BasisNotAvailable, ReplicaUnavailable).
    m1 an exception after the fsync fails the broker and answers
       outcome-unknown; the decision loop cannot leak a rejection.
    m5/m6 receipts record QLEVER_COMMIT_PATH; the P3 harness records
       per-position source, ACK and consumer instants and fails on gaps.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

