388:| Q58a native-query tokens (provisional, replaces Q55c's native half; flagged for Sam) | Native queries go through a Triplex facade; engine ports are not a public surface. A request may carry `after: position` (wait until the replica marker reaches it within the deadline, then typed BasisNotAvailable{required, observed, replica}) or `at: position` (exact; also requires the engine to reconstruct it, else typed BasisNotReconstructible). A client session sends its own high-water mark (last commit position and last read basis) as an implicit `after`. Tokenless external callers get the replica's watermark and the reported position. Every answer carries {basis: {low, high}, route}. Replica unreachable stays ReplicaUnavailable. Default deadline 2 s. | R23 sections 2 and 7; mature systems (Mongo, Cosmos, XTDB client, LiteFS) |
389:| Q58b EXP-P2B | XTDB becomes a second replica behind the broker: one pgwire transaction per frame (ASSERT the marker, INSERT rows with a fixed `_valid_from`, INSERT the new marker; P0004 on guard failure); rows and marker read in one read-only transaction; the marker row is the eligibility authority; XTDB system time is not used to carry broker positions; Local log first, InMemory log plus an epoch bump as an arm; predictions and measurements per R23 section 6. It starts after the broker fix round (Q62) is re-verified, from the same author, so one writer owns the broker files. | R23 section 6; Q51b |
390:| Q58c broker substrate (hardening experiment after P2B) | The host log moves to SQLite through better-sqlite3 (WAL, synchronous=FULL, fullfsync=ON, checkpoint_fullfsync=ON, locking_mode=EXCLUSIVE, application-driven PASSIVE checkpoints, a worker thread when readers share the process), keeping a CRC32C prev-chain column, a `committed_at` column, an epoch row and the marker and checkpoint cross-checks (plain SQLite misses mid-WAL corruption). heads, claims and operations become tables; the overlay becomes a persisted `recent_rows` table. Predictions H1-H6 of R23 section 6.4. This replaces Q50d's rotation and lock items. | R23 section 3; Q50d |
391:| Q58d overlay rules | The overlay merge is allowed for entity pulls only, keyed by id with the greater LSN winning, under a tested invariant (identity columns never change; retraction is a new version). Engine aggregates, Datalog and executor reads and paged lists never merge: they wait or fail typed. Frames carry explicit tombstones so erasure and deletes cannot resurrect replica rows. | R23 section 5 |
392:| Q58e erasure reaches the log | Values held in the broker log, `recent_rows` and checkpoints must be erasable: value payloads in frames are encrypted per subject and erasure destroys the key (crypto-shredding), so TARGETS 7 holds without rewriting the log. Design in the hardening experiment. | R23 open question 4; TARGETS 7 |
399:| Q59c verification briefs | Every verification and re-check saves its own BRIEF file, so the registry's brief hash identifies the actual instructions. | Q55a |
