     1	# EXP-P2Q QLever behind a host log and broker: report (saved by the orchestrator, 2026-11-07 22:50Z)
     2	
     3	**Bottom line:** the candidate (option `broker`, default off; A0 unchanged) ACKs independently of QLever's delta. In every paired window on
     4	the shared dev resident the candidate ACKed in 4 to 8 ms p50 while A0 took 0.96 to 7.4 s; read-your-own-write held on every completed pull;
     5	the feed and the Q31c falsifiers pass. The controlled delta-level measurements need an exclusive slot and did not run (pool at 10.0 of 11 GiB
     6	all session). Branch `exp/P2Q-qlever-log-broker` head d7c6086 (384d634, 2b73620, 650b18f, d7c6086); not merged pending verification.
     7	
     8	## Design
     9	- Frames per R13 2.4 (32-byte headers, CRC32C chain, torn-tail truncation with a backup copy, refusal on mid-log corruption); kinds
    10	  COMMIT_GROUP and EPOCH_BEGIN; quads are a pure function of the rows; delete terms from the broker's own encoder, never read back.
    11	- Positions (Q31c): (stream = scope, epoch, offset = LSN, ordinal) packed as lsn*1024 + ordinal; an EPOCH_BEGIN on every open; a torn tail
    12	  burns its LSN (the abort gap); every position at or below the head is resolved.
    13	- ACK after fsync and the watermark update (Q31e). Claims and per-subject CAS (read and write sets), escalating to a scope-wide check for
    14	  reads not tied to known entities; group commit of everything queued during the previous fsync (up to 64, no timer).
    15	- Asynchronous publication: up to 64 commands per guarded update on a fresh connection with a (broker_position, broker_epoch) marker guard;
    16	  a higher epoch means fail-stop; a lower marker means replay from the log.
    17	- Overlay eligibility: one SPARQL request returns rows and marker; the replica answers when its marker has reached B, else the overlay is
    18	  merged if it still holds every frame after the marker, else the read goes to the log; temporal filters in the kernel.
