   172	## 4. Window rejection
   173	Signals per round at 10 s cadence (collector `R22/collect-vm.sh`, read-only, tens of ms of guest CPU; host: `sysctl -n vm.loadavg
   174	kern.memorystatus_vm_pressure_level vm.swapusage`, `vm_stat`, `top -l 1 -n 0 | grep 'CPU usage'` at most every 30 s).
   175	| Signal | Source | Ambient today [M] | Class | Provisional rule |
   176	| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
   177	| Host load average | `sysctl vm.loadavg` | 11 to 15 | record only | never discriminates here |
   178	| Host CPU idle | `top -l 1` | 1.65% | record only | same |
   179	| Host memory pressure level | `kern.memorystatus_vm_pressure_level` | 2 | hard at 4 | exclude at CRITICAL |
   180	| Swap used | `vm.swapusage` | 96% | hard on growth | exclude if pageouts rise by more than 20,000 pages in a round |
   181	| Compressor, decompressions | `vm_stat` | 16 G, 1.8e9 total | record | calibrate during the recording week |
   182	| VM steal | `/proc/stat` | 0 | drop | unavailable |
   183	| VM PSI cpu some | `/proc/pressure/cpu` | 22 to 25% | soft | amber above 40%, exclude above 60% |
   184	| VM PSI memory full | same | about 0 | hard | exclude above 1% of round time |
   185	| VM PSI io some | same | below 0.2% | soft | exclude above 10% |
   186	| Throttled-period share per arm | cgroup `cpu.stat` | 0 to 77% (quota) | hard in cpuset regime | exclude above 5% on a cpuset arm |
   187	| Memory limit pressure | `memory.events` | `max` events in thousands on one slot | hard | exclude if `oom_kill` rises, a container restarts, or `max` rises by more than 50 |
   188	| Neighbor CPU | other cgroups' `usage_usec` | 1.75 to 3.7 cores | hard after partition | exclude if a non-arm container on an arm's cpuset exceeds 0.25 cores |
   189	| Calibration drift | pre and post spin | min varies 9% | hard | exclude if post/pre min is outside [0.85, 1.18] |
   190	| Interference index | p50/min of the spin | 1.1 to 1.36 | hard | exclude above 2.0 |
   191	| Hiccup meter (1 ms sleep overshoot) | driver and VM | max 4 to 9 ms per 4 s | hard | exclude above 100 ms |
   192	| Client event-loop use | driver ELU | existing | hard | above 0.9 (already INVALID) |
   193	Rules are decided before looking at outcomes, applied to both arms of a round, logged by rule id; a window is INVALID if more than a third
   194	of its rounds are excluded; thresholds are provisional until a 7-day passive recording at 10 s sets them at the 90th percentile of the
   195	signals that predict the A/A spread.
   196	
   197	**Outcome-based gate.** Per A/A round d_k = ln(p50_A / p50_B), s_d = sd(d_k):
   198	| Target R | Rounds allowed | s_d limit |
   199	| --- | --- | --- |
   200	| 1.25 | 12 | 0.28 |
   201	| 1.25 | 24 | 0.39 |
   202	| 1.10 | 24 | 0.17 |
   203	Above the 24-round limit the window is RED and discarded. The 3-round pre-flight catches only gross noise: use a safety factor of 1.5 on its
   204	s_d and refresh from interleaved A/A rounds. The A/A mean of d_k estimates slot bias; if its interval excludes 0, swap roles with a restart
   205	or correct for it.
   206	
   207	**Calibration.** 20 units of about 20 ms fixed integer work before and after each round, on the host and in the VM (python via `colima ssh`,
   208	about 0.45 s each); record min, p50, p50/min; reference = min of the first 5 pre-flight runs (stable within 9% while p50 moved 21%; minimum
   209	timing is robust when noise is additive [S, Chen and Revels; BenchmarkTools]); hiccup meter during blocks (jHiccup [S]). MongoDB runs non-MongoDB
   210	canaries beside every performance task and targets an experiment range (max - min) / median under 10% with 25 points per experiment; storage
   211	and CPU-option changes cut their run-to-run variation from 20-30% to under 5% [S].
